Why the Lesser one
------------------

Cheetah is a library that other programs build into themselves. Under
the ordinary GPL, every program that embedded it would have to be
GPL-compatible as a whole. Under the Lesser license anyone may embed
it, whatever their own program is licensed under, while changes to
Cheetah itself stay free. That is the arrangement this project wants:
the engine stays open, the programs using it are none of its business.


The code inherited from Cheetah3
--------------------------------

Cheetah Template 4 is a fork of Cheetah3, which is under the MIT
license. That permission is not withdrawn and cannot be: the code
inherited from Cheetah3 remains available under the MIT license from
its own project, and its notice is reproduced in full below, as the
MIT license requires.

Which is which can be read off the directories:

    Cheetah/        inherited from Cheetah3 and modified here
    ct4/            written for this project
    tests/          written for this project
    corpus/         see the section at the end

The relicensing applies to the work as distributed here. Anyone who
prefers the MIT terms will find them upstream:

    https://github.com/CheetahTemplate3/cheetah3


